  "term": "cardiac muscle",
  "definition": "Cardiac muscle is the excitable muscle tissue of the heart. In the packet, it is described as tissue whose electrical activity is shaped by voltage-gated potassium channels that help control repolarization and the timing of action potentials, so channel dysfunction can contribute to arrhythmias.",
