      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that cardiac muscle is an excitable tissue involved in cardiac electrical activity, but it does not explicitly define cardiac muscle as “the excitable muscle tissue of the heart.”",
        "The definition adds a general explanatory framing (“In the packet, it is described as…”) rather than a direct dictionary-style sense; this is not a standalone definition.",
        "The supported packet claim is narrower: Kv channels contribute to repolarization in excitable tissues such as cardiac muscle and their dysfunction can be associated with cardiac disorders with arrhythmias, but the definition overstates this as a definitional property of cardiac muscle itself."
